  "details": "I've noticed that the AnimatorPlayAudio state behaviour seems to be allowed on Android avatars despite AudioSources being blocked. This seems to include the referenced audio files in the builds, taking up valuable space.\n\nIdeally AudioSources simply get stripped/disabled as well, but those are much less of a hassle to remove manually than the state behaviours.\n\nI discovered this while making an optimised version of the SyncDances prefab as a personal challenge, where I used a large amount of AnimatorPlayAudio states to control one Audio Source. The Android version ended up at 26MB download size until I manually removed the state behaviours, after which it dropped to 16MB.",
